.TH RUM-METER 1 "2026-11-01" "rum-meter 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rum-meter \- Estimate billable HCP Terraform RUM from local state files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
Usage: rum-meter [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
Usage: rum-meter count [OPTIONS] <STATE>...
Usage: rum-meter diff [OPTIONS] <OLD> <NEW>
Usage: rum-meter help [COMMAND]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Estimate billable HCP Terraform RUM from local state files.
.PP
.B count
Count billable RUM in one or more state files.
Each
.I STATE
is a state file, or - to read stdin.
.PP
.B diff
Compare billable RUM in two state files.
.I OLD
is the earlier state file, or - to read stdin.
.I NEW
is the later state file, or - to read stdin.
.PP
.B help
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s).
An optional
.I COMMAND
prints help for that subcommand.
The help text for
.B help
itself says: Print help for the subcommand(s).
.B rum-meter help
prints the same text as
.B rum-meter --help
and exits 0.
.B rum-meter help count
prints the same text as
.B rum-meter count --help
and exits 0.
.B rum-meter help diff
prints the same text as
.B rum-meter diff --help
and exits 0.
.B rum-meter help help
prints the help command's own text and exits 0.
That text names no options.
The word after
.B help
is a command name, so
.B rum-meter help --help
exits 3 and reports an unrecognized subcommand.
.PP
A state file has to be Terraform state format version 4, and the root value has to be a JSON object.
The program reads the paths it is given.
It reads stdin only when a state argument is - and stdin is a pipe or a regular file.
A price file is always a path.
.B --prices -
is not stdin.
The program makes no network connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.B rum-meter --help
and
.B rum-meter -h
list the options below and exit 0.
.B rum-meter count --help
and
.B rum-meter diff --help
list the same options except
.BR --version ,
and exit 0.
.B -h
is the short form of
.B --help
on the top level, on
.B count
and on
.BR diff .
.B -V
is the short form of
.B --version
and is accepted on the top level only.
.TP
.B --json
Print JSON instead of text.
.TP
.B --explain
Print one line per instance.
On
.B diff
the flag changes the report only together with
.BR --json .
.TP
.B --top <N>
List at most N modules and N resource types.
On
.B diff
the flag changes the report only together with
.BR --json .
.TP
.B --prices <FILE>
Read tier prices from this JSON file.
.TP
.B --hours-per-month <N>
Hours in a month for the cost estimate.
The default is 730.
The flag changes the report only together with
.BR --prices .
.TP
.B --max-rum <N>
RUM limit for count.
The report is still printed.
The exit status is 1 when the summed RUM is greater than N.
N itself is success.
.TP
.B --max-increase <N>
RUM increase limit for diff.
The report is still printed.
The exit status is 1 when new RUM minus old RUM is greater than N.
An equal increase is success.
A decrease is success.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version.
.B rum-meter --version
and
.B rum-meter -V
print
.B rum-meter 1.0.0
and exit 0.
.B count --version
and
.B diff --version
are unexpected arguments and exit 3.
.PP
A flag that would not change the report exits 3, with one fixed line on stderr and nothing on stdout, before any file is read.
The same lines end the text of
.BR rum-meter\ --help ,
.B count --help
and
.BR diff\ --help .
If several apply, the first of these wins:
.PP
.nf
--max-increase only works with diff
--max-rum only works with count
--hours-per-month only works together with --prices
--top with diff only works together with --json
--explain with diff only works together with --json
.fi
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.B --help
and
.B --version
exit 0 when their text can be written.
A count or a diff that finishes exits 0, including when the total or the increase is equal to the threshold.
.TP
.B 1
A threshold is exceeded.
.B --max-rum
on
.B count
when the summed RUM is greater than N, or
.B --max-increase
on
.B diff
when the RUM increase is greater than N.
The report is still printed.
.TP
.B 2
An input error.
That includes an unreadable file, a path that is not a regular file, invalid JSON, a state that is not a JSON object, a state version other than 4, a duplicate address, the same state file given more than once, UTF-16 or UTF-32, an invalid price file, a monthly cost that overflows, a file larger than 128 MiB, or a resource label repeated across too many instances (a 32 MiB shared label budget).
Stdout is empty for these errors.
A report that cannot be written to stdout is also exit 2, with
.BR "rum-meter: cannot write report to stdout" .
Some of the report may already have been written.
.B --version
and
.B --help
that cannot be written are exit 2, not 0, with
.BR "rum-meter: cannot write message to stdout" .
A failed write does not panic.
.TP
.B 3
A usage error.
An unknown option, a missing argument, and a flag that would not change the report are exit 3.
Stdout is empty.
.SH EXAMPLES
.I examples/one-managed.tfstate
in this repository is a fictional Terraform state of format version 4.
It is not a state file from this machine.
It has one managed
.I random_id.handbook
instance.
From the repository root the command exits 0 and prints:
.PP
.nf
$ rum-meter count examples/one-managed.tfstate
file: examples/one-managed.tfstate
rum: 1
not counted: R2 0, R3 0, R4 0
total rum: 1
not counted: R2 0, R3 0, R4 0
modules:
  (root): 1
types:
  random_id: 1
estimate: HCP Terraform bills the hourly peak; this is a single snapshot
.fi
.PP
These commands exit 0:
.PP
.nf
$ rum-meter --help
$ rum-meter -h
$ rum-meter --version
$ rum-meter -V
$ rum-meter count --help
$ rum-meter diff --help
$ rum-meter help
$ rum-meter help count
$ rum-meter help diff
$ rum-meter help help
.fi
.PP
.B rum-meter --version
prints:
.PP
.nf
rum-meter 1.0.0
.fi
